Adaptation note: pattern-level adaptation from CurryCaster v1 applies from
POD-08 / POD-15 onward — specifically the file library indexing model, the
cartwall model, the waveform/cue interaction model, and the MIDI mapper.
POD-08 (2026-11-18) landed the first four of these as adapted-pattern
components: the player engine (PlayerModule behaviour: 8 players, LRU
non-playing reuse, already-loaded flash, IN/OUT cues, STOP→IN, log fader,
played-dimming), the cartwall audio binding (CartWallWindow/CartButton
behaviour: click play/stop, per-cart fader, countdown, STOP ALL), the
waveform/cue interaction model (WaveformWidget behaviour on server peaks:
zoom/pan/click-seek, cue markers, dimming outside the cue region), and the
clip browser's library model. POD-15 (2026-11-18) landed the MIDI mapper
as an adapted-pattern component: the v1 MidiMapper/MidiWorker learn
behaviour (arm a control, move a knob / press a pad, the next message
binds; mappings persisted as JSON) rebuilt natively in TypeScript on
Web MIDI semantics in src/modules/podcast-studio/control/midi.ts, with
the keyboard action map alongside it in the same module family.
All are pattern-level adaptations — behaviour and interaction models
rebuilt natively in TypeScript; no CurryCaster v1 code is copied.
Earlier prompts (POD-00 … POD-07) do not adapt CurryCaster v1 code or
patterns; where their designs resemble CurryCaster behaviour, that behaviour
comes from the clean-room behavioural reference described in the provenance
register below.

